/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-106-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-107-  // ==== bin(n) — "0b" + binary digit codes (promoted from 103's defined fold) ==
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k:108:  rule applyBuiltin("bin", N:Int, .Vals) => str(iCons(48, iCons(98, binCodes(N))))
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-109-       requires N >=Int 0
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-110-  // negative operand: the '-' sign prefixes the magnitude's digits
