/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-276-  // ==== hashlib.md5(S).hexdigest() — a trusted opaque digest ==================
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-277-  // The md5 value itself is a named shared trust (sortVS-style, no concrete
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-278-  // twin); proofs use the length/hex-charset lemmas (lemmas/builtins.k).
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-279-  syntax KItem ::= "#md5"
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k:280:  rule <k> Call(Attribute(Name("hashlib"), "md5"), (E:Expr, .Exprs)) => E ~> #md5 ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/builtins.k-281-       [priority(40)]
