/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-3-// builtins at the root; a cooled Attribute is a bound method), evaluate the args (the shared
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-4-// #evalArgs loop in core.k), then dispatch on the callee value:
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-5-//   closureVal    -> bind params, push a frame (user function)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-6-//   boundMethodV  -> applyMethod
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:7://   builtinV      -> the #iterNext folds (sum/all/any/max/min) or applyBuiltin
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-8-//   typeV         -> callable type objects: int(...) / str(...)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-9-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-10-module MPY-CALL
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-11-  imports MPY-METHODS
--
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-16-  rule <k> Attribute(V:Val, M:String) => boundMethodV(V, M) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-17-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-18-  // evaluate callee, then args ([owise]: problem-local Call interceptions beat this)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-19-  syntax KItem ::= #callee(Exprs)
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:20:  rule <k> Call(Fe:Expr, ARGS:Exprs) => Fe ~> #callee(ARGS) ... </k> [owise]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:21:  rule <k> CV:Val ~> #callee(ARGS:Exprs) => #evalArgs(ARGS, .Vals, toCall(CV)) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-22-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-23-  // ==== dispatch on the callee value ========================================
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:24:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(boundMethodV(OBJ:Val, M:String)), ACC:Vals) => applyMethod(OBJ, M, ACC) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-25-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:26:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("sum")), (OBJ:Iterable, .Vals)) => #sumAcc(OBJ, 0) ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:27:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("all")), (OBJ:Iterable, .Vals)) => #allAcc(OBJ)    ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:28:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("any")), (OBJ:Iterable, .Vals)) => #anyAcc(OBJ)    ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:29:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("max")), (OBJ:Iterable, .Vals)) => #maxAcc0(OBJ)   ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:30:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("min")), (OBJ:Iterable, .Vals)) => #minAcc0(OBJ)   ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:31:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV(BN:String)), ACC:Vals) => applyBuiltin(BN, ACC) ... </k> [owise]
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k:32:  rule <k> #applyK(toCall(typeV(T:String)),     ACC:Vals) => applyBuiltin(T, ACC)  ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-33-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-34-  // ==== heap-object arguments/receivers =====================================
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-35-  // Builtins and type calls READ structure — deref the first two arg positions
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/call.k-36-  // (covers len/sum/all/any/max/min/sorted/list/set + zip's pair). Mutating list
